{
  "calm_space_method": "Semantic free-surface proxy, measured in native viewport pixels. Occupied mask is the union of visible nonempty text-control rectangles, card face rectangles, action-button rectangles, art frames, stat/cost badges and gold plaque. Remaining pixels are counted as calm; plain tray/playmat/shop surfaces and empty pockets count as calm. Masks are white=calm, black=occupied. Bounds use floor/ceil then clip to viewport. Mask region paths/rectangles are saved with each capture for audit.",
  "calm_space_limitations": "This measures free surface, not perceptual complexity: floor marks, tray carving and background grain are not separately subtracted; text rectangles include padding. It is an explicit, identical before/after proxy, not a claim that the perceptual 35-40% target passed. Reader-open rows are reported separately and are not resting-budget scenarios.",
